# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# forever/horde/04-the-barrens ends at Seereth's camp after Stonetalon: this guide opens with the walk east to the
# Crossroads' flight master (the hearth is kept for Splintertree Post's bind), and its Great Lift step takes
# Calling in the Reserves (5881, from Maggran at Sun Rock) to Grish Longrunner and Message to Freewind Post (4542)
# from Brave Moonhorn, both at the top of the lift.
# Added here: The Broodmother (96261), Hypercapacitor Gizmo (5151), The Tear of the Moons (857, a
# level 30 quest, at 28 on the road from Camp Taurajo to the Great Lift, #1333).
# Carried in from forever/horde/04-the-barrens' Thunder Bluff stop (or 06's for Druids), for players
# who took them: The Sacred Flame (1195: the Etched Phial from Raynewood's Laughing Sisters, filled at
# the moonwell south of them on the way to Mystral Lake; 1196 from Zangen on the Thunder Bluff stop to
# Rau at Freewind; 1197 at the Ancient Brazier in Splithoof Hold, north of the Galak camps) and
# Pigments for Paints (97538, Tah Winterhoof on the Thunder Bluff stop). Every step of theirs is shown
# only to a player carrying the quest. Everyone flies from Zoram'gar to Thunder Bluff (04 teaches the
# flight path; without it the arrow goes by Camp Taurajo and Mulgore).
# The Mirage Raceway's quests (1110, 1104, 5762, 1105, 1176, 1175, Martek the Exiled 1106) are worked in one
# visit at 33 in forever/horde/30-40/02-thousand-needles.
# Stonetalon Standstill (25) is taken from Mastok on the first Splintertree stop and worked at Mystral
# Lake with Tideress on the way back from Shadumbra: Tideress drops the Befouled Water Globe (The
# Befouled Element 1918) only for a player with 25 in the log or handed in (players' recordings, #1346).
# Troll Charm (6462), Between a Rock and a Thistlefur (216) and Freedom to Ruul (6482) are done on the
# first Ashenvale visit at 21 (forever/horde/05-stonetalon-mountains), with Vorsha the Lasher (6641); King of the Foulweald (6621)
# opens with 216's hand-in and is taken here from Karang.
# Ashenvale Outrunners (6503, level 24) is taken here at the Warsong lumber camp, between Torek's assault and
# Sharptalon in the same woods (0.3.7): on the first visit at 21-23 the model's players were 1-1.5 levels under it.
#
# Blackfathom Deeps (`when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"`, dungeons in the route): for a character who
# chose it, Je'neu's Amongst the Ruins (6921) is taken on the first Zoram'gar stop and the run follows the
# Sapphires, in the same tunnels as the portal, at about 27; the Strange Water Globe (6922) and the Damp Note (6564) start
# inside, and Je'neu takes all three at once (`when complete`/`when onquest`). Left out: Blackfathom
# Villainy (6561: Argent Guard Thaelrid gives it inside, a giver our data has no place for, and Bashana
# Runetotem takes it on the Elder Rise, off this guide's Thunder Bluff stop; the run tip names it),
# Allegiance to the Old Gods part 2 (6565, a second run) and the Warlock's Orb of Soran'ruk (1740, class guide).

step Fly to Zoram'gar Outpost
  zone The Barrens
  tip East along the road from Seereth's camp to the Crossroads' wind rider master, and fly to Zoram'gar Outpost. Keep your hearthstone: Splintertree Post's bind later in this guide saves more.
  goto 51.5,30.4 "Crossroads flight master"
  fly "Zoram'gar Outpost"
  zone Ashenvale

step Zoram'gar Outpost
  zone Ashenvale
  tip Je'neu Sancrea stands in the outpost.
  turnin 6562                         -- Je'neu Sancrea
  accept 6563

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"
  tip For your Blackfathom Deeps run, in the same tunnels as the Sapphires: Je'neu's ruins errand. Look for a group now if you have none yet.
  accept 6921                         -- Je'neu Sancrea

# The Sapphires (objects 178184-178186, 12.9-13.8,10.6-13.5) grow in the
# tunnels under the strand that lead to the Blackfathom Deeps portal, outside
# the instance: "Within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps, large
# sapphire clusters can be found along the cave walls" (the quest text), "the
# blue crystals that appear in the tunnels leading up to the instance, not
# inside the instance itself" and "go into the ruins and then down a bunch of
# stairs, swim under water to get to the other side of a wall"
# (players' reports, quest 6563). The way in is the
# ruins' pit at 14.5,14.2 (the client's Blackfathom Deeps entrance,
# dungeons.json; players report the entrance in the pit
# near 14,14, zone 719); a straight line from
# the brazier to the crystals ends on the strand above them.
step Blackfathom Deeps ruins
  tip The way to the Sapphires is through the sunken ruins at the north end of the strand: go down the stairs into the pit.
  goto 14.5,14.2 "Blackfathom Deeps ruins"

step Sapphires of Aku'Mai
  tip The Sapphires are blue crystals on the walls of the tunnels leading to the Blackfathom Deeps portal, underground and outside the instance: swim down from the pit, under the wall, into the cave. The satyrs and naga in the tunnels are elite: grouping up is advised. The crystals respawn quickly, so there is no need to go deep.
  collect 16784 quest 6563

step Blackfathom Deeps
  when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"
  when onquest 6921
  zone Ashenvale
  tip Blackfathom Deeps is a dungeon for a group of five, about levels 22 to 30, and a full run takes about an hour. Its portal is a little further along the tunnels you are in, past the Sapphires.
  tip Inside: the Fathom Stone lies under the water of the Moonshrine Ruins' pool, beneath the walkway (clear the crabs first): open it for the Fathom Core, and Baron Aquanis comes; open the Strange Water Globe he drops for a quest for Je'neu. The Tide Priestesses sometimes drop a Damp Note: open it for another quest for Je'neu. Argent Guard Thaelrid, by a campfire in an underwater side room off Ghamoo-ra's room, offers Blackfathom Villainy (Twilight Lord Kelris' head, for Bashana Runetotem on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise).
  enter "Blackfathom Deeps" @14.5,14.2
  complete 6921                       -- Amongst the Ruins: the Fathom Core, from the Fathom Stone

step Zoram'gar Outpost
  note Je'neu offers a Blackfathom Deeps quest next; leave it unless you have a group.
  tip Back to Zoram'gar from the ruins before heading east for good.
  turnin 6563                         -- Je'neu Sancrea
  accept 6621                         -- Karang Amakkar: a banner defence in the Foulweald, east of Mystral Lake: furbolg waves, then Chief Murgut

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"
  when complete 6921
  zone Ashenvale
  turnin 6921                         -- Je'neu Sancrea

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"
  when onquest 6922
  zone Ashenvale
  turnin 6922                         -- Je'neu Sancrea

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when dungeon "Blackfathom Deeps"
  when onquest 6564
  zone Ashenvale
  tip Je'neu then offers the next part, Allegiance to the Old Gods: it is for a second run, so leave it.
  turnin 6564                         -- Je'neu Sancrea

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- East along the road

step Ruins of Stardust fountain
  zone Ashenvale
  only Shaman
  tip The fountain stands in the middle of the Ruins of Stardust, where Ursangous roams: use the Empty Blue Waterskin there.
  collect 7770 quest 1534.1

step Ursangous
  when turnedin 6383
  tip Follow the main road east past Astranaar (Alliance: keep to the road). Ursangous, a big grizzly, roams the Ruins of Stardust south of the road, west of Mystral Lake. His paw starts the next hunt quest.
  collect 16303
  accept 23 item 16303

step King of the Foulweald
  tip The Foulweald furbolgs hold the woods east of Mystral Lake, south of the road. Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound and guard it: the furbolgs come to tear it down. Chief Murgut comes last; his totem drops in the basket.
  use 16972 quest 6621.1 @56.4,63.5 map 1440
  collect 16976 quest 6621

step Torek's Assault
  tip Keep east on the road. Torek waits south-west of the Warsong lumber camp. He and his grunts storm the Silverwing Outpost: let them take aggro and stay with Torek until Duriel Moonfire is dead.
  accept 6544
  complete 6544

step Warsong lumber camp
  tip From the Silverwing Outpost head north-east to the Warsong lumber camp on the road: Kuray'bin stands there.
  accept 6503                         -- Kuray'bin

step Ashenvale Outrunners
  tip The night elf Ashenvale Outrunners (23-24) stalk the woods south and south-east of the lumber camp; they stealth, so watch for them.
  kill 12856 quest 6503 @72.5,69.5 map 1440

step Warsong lumber camp
  tip Back to Kuray'bin at the lumber camp, on the road north to Splintertree.
  turnin 6503                         -- Kuray'bin

